{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/814016-masks","id":814016,"title":"Masks?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-22T03:00:16-08:00","id":814016,"title":"Masks?","content":"In second edition Changeling, do the Losts masks look like their old human identity or is it the closest human equivalent to the fairy mien. That is, the Changeling looks totally different from their original appearance. This would allow you to really explore the concept of beautiful lies Changeling. I also think it would allow you to explore some really cool concepts from 1E that were never really fully developed. 1). Family: Because the Changeling looks nothing like himself, he can\u2019t simply kill his fetch and move back into his old life. This would force the Changeling to confront what family means to them. what are they willing to sacrifice for it? What are they willing to do to get it back? 2). Fusing with your Fetch: Because most Changelings looked like their old identity and were little more then human, the players did not really need to explore the benefits and consequences of fusing with your Fetch. I also believe that having the Fetch look more and act more like the Changeling\u2019s human identity, it makes the Fetch a more critical antagonists to the Changeling\u2019s storyline. For example, Changeling\u2019s are hesitant to kill their fetch (as much as they want to), because fusing with the Fetch is the only way the Changeling can get back his old life. Note: Changeling\u2019s should suffer something similar to Mage\u2019s Paradox or Promethean\u2019s Disquiet that prevents them from using their blessings and contracts to force their way back into their old lives. Sometime\u2019s they have to, however, because the Fetch was going to kill their family or worse, give them to the Gentry. Or the Changeling may fuse with their Fetch only only to find that the Fetch had destroyed every personal connection important to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T03:01:45-08:00","id":814017,"title":"","content":"Giving the Losts new appearances would also allow the players to have more fun with their character\u2019s backgrounds. It would be interesting to show how a character acts when they gain a beauty they had never imagined in their mortal lives. This could include, A Fairest might have a been a Tyrion Lannister (Song of Ice and Fire) or an Agatha (The School For Good and Evil) who gained their beauty for their heroic acts. Or for the new Romancer/Succubus kith, the Gentry chose people who were plain or even downright homely because they wanted to be that person\u2019s prince/princess charming, or simply to corrupt their values.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T03:14:06-08:00","id":814018,"title":"","content":"I hope it's like 1e, where they look like themselves but altered within reason by their kith.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T08:35:27-08:00","id":814147,"title":"","content":"I like to think of the Mask as an extension of humanity's tendency to ignore the supernatural, amped up to 11 by the Wyrd. While I've never ST'd Lost, if I did, that interpretation would color the way I describe Masks. When a normal human in the CofD sees an elemental with a flaming head just walking around, running errands, he rationalizes her as a &quot;flaming&quot; redhead. When he passes a Beast on the street, he avoids eye contact with what he assumes is a homeless man with a thick beard and a fur-lined coat. He's far too polite to say anything about the big and tall man in line at the DMV (who is actually an eight foot Ogre).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 01-22-2016, 11:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T09:54:51-08:00","id":814203,"title":"","content":"Masks operate like they used to in Changeling First Edition.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Okay, not true, the reinforcing and dropping mechanics are different, and you have a few motives to drop your Mask now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T10:34:23-08:00","id":814240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/814016-masks?p=814203#post814203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Masks operate like they used to in Changeling First Edition.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Okay, not true, the reinforcing and dropping mechanics are different, and you have a few motives to drop your Mask now.</div> </div> </div> </div> Cool, the old rules were too punishing if you wanted to drop your mask, using up all your current glamour, with the exception of the vainglory contracts.<br /> <br /> Also I think that the Fae Touched template spoiler hinted at this under the merit that granted a Mein to the Fae Touched.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T14:56:57-08:00","id":814470,"title":"","content":"I wonder if reinforcing will be more expensive, I had a character who tried to reinforce his mask whenever he went out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T03:25:47-08:00","id":815340,"title":"","content":"So maybe dropping your Mask to reveal your Mien is the changeling equivalent of releasing auras? That'd be interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5789-acanthus",